WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.833
(crowd cheering)

00:00:00.833 --> 00:00:04.030
- [Narrator] With 149
million customers worldwide,

00:00:04.030 --> 00:00:05.630
it's no secret that Netflix

00:00:05.630 --> 00:00:08.300
is the world champion of streaming video.

00:00:08.300 --> 00:00:09.133
(bell dings)

00:00:09.133 --> 00:00:11.430
But new competitors are entering the ring,

00:00:11.430 --> 00:00:15.520
among them Comcast, AT&amp;T, and Disney.

00:00:15.520 --> 00:00:18.420
Now, those traditional
media giants are gearing up

00:00:18.420 --> 00:00:21.280
to launch subscription
streaming services of their own,

00:00:21.280 --> 00:00:24.080
entering a crowded field alongside Amazon,

00:00:24.080 --> 00:00:28.240
Hulu, Apple, and others, and
they're ready to duke it out

00:00:28.240 --> 00:00:31.870
for who will distribute your
favorite movies and TV shows.

00:00:31.870 --> 00:00:33.940
- I say bring it on!

00:00:33.940 --> 00:00:36.070
- [Narrator] Netflix is no ordinary foe.

00:00:36.070 --> 00:00:39.060
It spends $12 billion a year on content,

00:00:39.060 --> 00:00:42.850
and it's a magnet for top
Hollywood producers and actors,

00:00:42.850 --> 00:00:44.350
but most importantly,

00:00:44.350 --> 00:00:46.673
it has a head start of more than a decade,

00:00:47.920 --> 00:00:50.360
but the three new entrants
have a secret weapon,

00:00:50.360 --> 00:00:53.800
TV brands and movie franchises
people know and love.

00:00:53.800 --> 00:00:56.270
They've licensed a lot of
their classic programming

00:00:56.270 --> 00:00:59.160
to Netflix over the years, but now,

00:00:59.160 --> 00:01:02.310
they'll wanna bring their hits
back to their own services,

00:01:02.310 --> 00:01:04.720
and that could pose a
challenge to Netflix.

00:01:04.720 --> 00:01:07.887
(rhythmic rock music)

00:01:09.860 --> 00:01:12.070
First up, Comcast.

00:01:12.070 --> 00:01:15.120
Comcast Corp.'s NBCUniversal
has plans to launch

00:01:15.120 --> 00:01:18.410
an ad-supported streaming service by 2020.

00:01:18.410 --> 00:01:20.103
- You need to play to win,

00:01:21.610 --> 00:01:26.610
but you also have to win to play.

00:01:28.350 --> 00:01:29.650
- [Narrator] The company hasn't said much

00:01:29.650 --> 00:01:31.500
about what will be on the service,

00:01:31.500 --> 00:01:33.470
but viewers can expect lots of content

00:01:33.470 --> 00:01:36.630
from their film and TV franchises.

00:01:36.630 --> 00:01:38.790
Executives are already
contemplating bringing back

00:01:38.790 --> 00:01:41.580
The Office, Netflix's most-watched show,

00:01:41.580 --> 00:01:44.590
since the contract expires in 2021.

00:01:44.590 --> 00:01:46.180
Parks and Recreation is another show

00:01:46.180 --> 00:01:48.003
Comcast might wanna fight for.

00:01:49.330 --> 00:01:51.190
An ad-supported service will be available

00:01:51.190 --> 00:01:54.720
to around 54 million customers
that already subscribe

00:01:54.720 --> 00:01:57.910
to Comcast Cable and Sky
and other cable providers

00:01:57.910 --> 00:02:01.640
that offer NBC channels, and
those without traditional

00:02:01.640 --> 00:02:05.243
pay TV packages will be able
to subscribe for a monthly fee,

00:02:06.260 --> 00:02:08.700
but to be competitive,
Comcast may also need

00:02:08.700 --> 00:02:11.620
to pump some cash into
original programming,

00:02:11.620 --> 00:02:14.454
but will that be enough
to challenge Netflix?

00:02:14.454 --> 00:02:16.570
(bell dings)

00:02:16.570 --> 00:02:17.640
The next challenger?

00:02:17.640 --> 00:02:20.717
AT&amp;T's Warner Media.
(rousing electro rock music)

00:02:20.717 --> 00:02:24.630
AT&amp;T's recent acquisition of
Time Warner, now WarnerMedia,

00:02:24.630 --> 00:02:27.350
means the company has bulked
up into a major producer

00:02:27.350 --> 00:02:29.780
of film and television content,

00:02:29.780 --> 00:02:32.223
home to the Warner
Brothers Studio and HBO.

00:02:33.200 --> 00:02:34.690
With movies like The Dark Knight

00:02:34.690 --> 00:02:36.920
and shows like Game of
Thrones in their corner,

00:02:36.920 --> 00:02:38.690
they could prove to be a major contender

00:02:38.690 --> 00:02:40.590
in the streaming ring.

00:02:40.590 --> 00:02:43.040
WarnerMedia streaming
service is expected to launch

00:02:43.040 --> 00:02:46.650
late this year with
content from HBO, Cinemax,

00:02:46.650 --> 00:02:49.570
Warner Brothers, and original programming.

00:02:49.570 --> 00:02:52.490
Warner chose to keep licensing
reruns of Friends to Netflix

00:02:52.490 --> 00:02:55.760
through 2019, but Warner has
the right to take the show back

00:02:55.760 --> 00:02:57.840
once it launches the new service.

00:02:57.840 --> 00:02:59.670
The company previously had a three-tiered

00:02:59.670 --> 00:03:02.770
pricing plan in mind, but
after reviewing the landscape,

00:03:02.770 --> 00:03:04.960
chose to pivot before launch.

00:03:04.960 --> 00:03:07.964
- Pivot!
(audience laughing)

00:03:07.964 --> 00:03:08.797
Pivot!

00:03:10.200 --> 00:03:11.650
- [Narrator] The last challenger?

00:03:11.650 --> 00:03:12.770
Disney.

00:03:12.770 --> 00:03:14.870
Before long, Disney will be operating

00:03:14.870 --> 00:03:17.520
three separate video streaming services,

00:03:17.520 --> 00:03:22.000
Hulu, ESPN+, and a new
streaming service called Disney+

00:03:22.000 --> 00:03:24.700
set to launch in November 2019.

00:03:24.700 --> 00:03:27.720
The company said is plans to
price the new Disney+ service

00:03:27.720 --> 00:03:31.200
at $6.99 a month, almost half the cost

00:03:31.200 --> 00:03:32.380
of a Netflix subscription.

00:03:32.380 --> 00:03:34.647
- In my call, that's a good fight.

00:03:34.647 --> 00:03:37.220
- [Narrator] Disney+ will
be anchored by programming

00:03:37.220 --> 00:03:40.670
from Disney's biggest
franchises, including Star Wars,

00:03:40.670 --> 00:03:42.960
Marvel Studios, and original programming,

00:03:42.960 --> 00:03:44.880
and Disney brought in other big titles

00:03:44.880 --> 00:03:48.340
like The Simpsons from its
$71 billion acquisition

00:03:48.340 --> 00:03:51.273
of 21st Century Fox's
entertainment assets.

00:03:52.330 --> 00:03:55.310
- Now, family, put on the mouse ears.

00:03:55.310 --> 00:03:59.130
You only get one chance to
make a first impression.

00:03:59.130 --> 00:04:01.120
- [Narrator] Now, Disney
is aggressively removing

00:04:01.120 --> 00:04:04.330
its top programming from
Netflix, but that move means

00:04:04.330 --> 00:04:08.070
losing $150 million a
year in operating income,

00:04:08.070 --> 00:04:09.480
which Disney hopes to recoup

00:04:09.480 --> 00:04:11.533
in subscription fees from Disney+.

00:04:13.690 --> 00:04:15.960
The challengers will be
working hard to get Netflix

00:04:15.960 --> 00:04:17.140
on the ropes,
(bell dings)

00:04:17.140 --> 00:04:18.880
but a big challenge will be making up

00:04:18.880 --> 00:04:21.130
for the hundreds of
millions of dollars loss

00:04:21.130 --> 00:04:23.610
from licensing programs to Netflix.

00:04:23.610 --> 00:04:25.930
That means signing up lots of customers

00:04:25.930 --> 00:04:27.980
and keeping Wall Street happy,

00:04:27.980 --> 00:04:29.622
easier said than done.

00:04:29.622 --> 00:04:33.205
(rhythmic hard rock music)

